{
  "title": "Telangiectatic Intramedullary Osteosarcoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8017/telangiectatic-intramedullary-osteosarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 8 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Telangiectatic Osteosarcomas are rare, malignant, high-grade osteosarcomas that occur most commonly in the proximal humerus, the femur, and proximal tibia. Patients typically present between the ages of 5 and 25 with regional pain and swelling.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with biopsy showing high-grade sarcoma with mitotic figures is seen in intervening cellular areas and lakes of blood mixed with malignant cells.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually neo-adjuvant chemotherapy, limb salvage surgical resection, followed by adjuvant chemotherapy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare (4% of osteosarcomas)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male > female",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "proximal humerus, proximal femur, distal femur, proximal tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occur in **same location as ABC**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history of prior radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
